      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In a multicenter study involving the five Orthopaedic Services of the COC, 57 patients with Kienböck's disease were reviewed 90% were treated surgically. The most common operations were ulna lengthening (30 cases) and lunate resection (11 cases). The most frequent indications or surgery were pain and stiffness of the wrist. Radiological changes are classified according to Decoulx. For evaluating post-operative radiological changes, however, the authors use different criteria ulna lengthening and lunate resection improved pain and mobility in 75% of cases. This study shows that lunate resection is a valid operation in the treatment of Kienböck's disease."},
